Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:40:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(toolpath):=20the=20RFC's=20signature=20alg?=
 =?UTF-8?q?orithm,=20proven=20=E2=80=94=20JCS=20inputs,=20SHA-256=20digest?=
 =?UTF-8?q?s,=20ssh=20verification?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A 'verify' feature on toolpath: v1::sign::{jcs, digest, step_author_input,
path_author_input, path_reviewer_input, verify_step_signature,
verify_path_signatures}. JCS is written in the crate (ECMAScript numbers
via ryu-js); ssh Ed25519 SSHSIG in namespace 'toolpath'; gpg/sigstore
refused. Tests: the six RFC 8785 reference vectors (vendored, Apache-2.0),
escapes, numbers, the RFC example byte for byte, what gets signed, JSONL
round trip, 2000 generated values; 14 signature tests with seeded keys.

serde_json float_roundtrip workspace-wide changes how every crate parses
floats: without it the RFC 8785 vectors canonicalize wrong and Claude
Code's costUSD 0.020428699999999998 silently read back as 0.0204287.
ir@/document@/shed@claude-session recaptured for that value only.

Gates build with toolpath/verify. Qualifier records on RFC.md 395 and
712-836 (RFC.md:719 is false: RFC 8785 orders keys by UTF-16, not
UTF-8), jsonl.rs, and examples/path-02 (its jsonl twin differs).
Record: pr/29-signatures.
